# System information (D69, D76, D77). The values belong to the machine, so
# only their shape is shown.
get environment variable "OS" into os
get system information "os" into system
say system
if length of name of system is greater than 0
    say "the system has a name"
.
if length of version of system is greater than 0
    say "and a version"
.
say architecture of system
if machineName of system is gone
    say "no machine name"
otherwise
    say "a machine name"
.
get system information "CPU" into cpu
say cpu
if cores of cpu is at least 1
    say "at least one core"
.
if os is "Windows_NT"
    if length of name of cpu is greater than 0
        say "the processor has a name"
    .
otherwise
    say "processor name:" name of cpu
.
get system information "memory" into memory
say memory
if totalBytes of memory is gone
    say "no memory figures"
otherwise if totalBytes of memory is at least freeBytes of memory
    say "free memory fits in total memory"
.
get system information "disk" into disk
say disk
if drive of disk is gone
    say "no drive"
otherwise if totalBytes of disk is at least freeBytes of disk
    say "free space fits on the disk"
.
get system information "network" into network
for each face in network
    if name of face is gone
        say "an interface with no name"
    .
.
say "network is a list"
get system information "groups" into groups
for each group in groups
    if length of group is 0
        say "a group with no name"
    .
.
say "groups is a list"
get system information "software" into software
for each app in software
    if name of app is gone
        say "an application with no name"
    .
.
say "software is a list"
get system information "services" into services
for each service in services
    if name of service is gone
        say "a service with no name"
    .
    if status of service is gone
        say "a service with no status"
    .
.
say "services is a list"
try
    get system information "user" into user
    say user
    if length of name of user is greater than 0
        say "the user has a name"
    .
    if isAdmin of user is true or isAdmin of user is false
        say "admin or not"
    .
otherwise into reason
    say reason
.
try
    get system information "weather" into nothing
otherwise into reason
    say reason
.
